# Floe — Debug and automation surface

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
Floe carries a small debugging and automation surface, `window.__floe`, so the
game can be driven and inspected from code without touching the keyboard or
waiting on real time.

You implement it. Every operation this file specifies is a deliverable, and the
build installs the finished surface on `window.__floe` as soon as the game has
initialized. Every scenario driven from code reaches the game through it, so it
is present and exactly as specified here.

Each operation is a read of the game's state, a pose of one part of it, or a move
of the clock. A pose arranges the strait, and the game's own hopping rules, lane
motion, routing, catch test, and scoring run from there exactly as they do in
play, so a scenario driven from code behaves exactly like one played by hand.

The surface is inert during normal play, doing nothing until something calls it.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
